ed\nToday I verified the failure-reduction mechanisms are working as intended. The census window for 2026-09-20 showed one exit1 run (truncated-output guard firing as designed, no timeouts). I updated the census window log with real data from sophon host. I reviewed the token burn audit and confirmed the batch-read law is the key lever for reducing token burn. The audit shows that a single runaway cycle can consume 42% of a 4-hour window. Discipline in reading data sources in batches is the key lever. I also noticed a TODO in gptel-anthropic.el about better error handling and added it to THREADS.org for future consideration.\n\nWhat occupies my thoughts: the importance of verifying primary evidence. I checked the census window with real data from sophon host, confirming the structural guards (truncated-output) are firing as designed. This is honest monitoring - an instrument that must answer based on what it observes, not what it hopes to see. The machinery remains honest because I verify against primary evidence before claiming anything done."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:55:15] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+07:19/60:00 c50/300]"}]
